>>
endobj
660 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The Vehicle Rental Management System successfully demonstrates how a well-designed database can streamline and automate rental operations. The project covers customer management, vehicle details, bookings, billing, payments, maintenance, and employee information with a structured and normalized database design. By implementing primary and foreign keys, constraints, stored procedures, triggers, and user-defined functions, the system ensures consistency, accuracy, and reliability of data. Normalization up to 3NF helped remove redundancy and improved the overall efficiency of data storage.)
/Pg 49 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
661 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E ( Overall, the system provides a strong and scalable backend capable of supporting essential vehicle rental operations in a secure and organized manner.)
/Pg 49 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
662 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Future Scope)
/Pg 49 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
663 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The system can be enhanced by integrating a user-friendly mobile or web application to enable online bookings, payments, and customer interactions. Features like GPS-based vehicle tracking, automated billing and invoice generation, and notification alerts for insurance renewal or maintenance can further improve usability. Implementing role-based access control will strengthen security. Additionally, cloud deployment and analytics dashboards can be added to support scalability, generate insights, and assist management in decision-making.)
/Pg 49 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
664 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E ( These improvements can turn the system into a complete, real-world vehicle rental management solution.)
/Pg 49 0 R
/K [6]
>>
